{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Water shall flow from his branches.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): מדליו — his branches, that is, the limbs." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> יזל מים מדליו — be watchful over the children of the poor, for from them Torah shall go forth, as it is said, יזל מים מדליו; and 'water' is nothing but Torah, as it is said (Isaiah 55:1): ״הוי כל צמא לכו למים״ — מדליו, from the poor (דלים) among them." "<b>And his seed in abundant waters.</b> He waters it with abundant waters, and it grows and sprouts every day, in the manner that Isaiah, peace be upon him, said concerning the prosperity of Israel (Isaiah 17:11): ״ביום נטעך תשגשגי ובבקר זרעך תפריחי״." "<b>And his king shall be higher than Agag.</b> This is Saul, who was the first king. And it says מאגג — on account of the matter that Saul captured Agag king of Amalek."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:45.412147640Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}